WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.463
Why GitHub Actions?

2
00:00:01.463 --> 00:00:04.536
Learn documents two ways
to run a scheduled job

3
00:00:04.536 --> 00:00:07.374
that signs in to Azure
with no stored secret.

4
00:00:07.374 --> 00:00:10.362
The chapter picks GitHub
Actions for three reasons.

5
00:00:10.362 --> 00:00:13.615
Learn publishes complete
sample workflows for it,

6
00:00:13.615 --> 00:00:15.938
including the US Government sign-in.

7
00:00:15.938 --> 00:00:20.100
The sign-in action is Microsoft's
own, with its source published.

8
00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:22.492
And for the other option, Azure Pipelines,

9
00:00:22.492 --> 00:00:25.587
the automatic setup doesn't
work in Azure Government.

10
00:00:25.587 --> 00:00:27.653
For this estate either would do,

11
00:00:27.653 --> 00:00:32.262
but one path that also documents the
higher clouds is easier to hand on.

12
00:00:32.262 --> 00:00:35.830
And the comparator and packager
work the same under either.
